# Homework 5 - Gradient Descent and Learning Rate Comparison

This assignment extends the regression work from Homework 4 by focusing on how gradient descent learns a simple linear regression model and how different learning rates affect convergence.

The analysis uses:

- `Advertising_Spend` as the predictor
- `Sales_Revenue` as the target

## Objectives
- Load and prepare the Homework 4 business dataset
- Use an 80/20 train-test split
- Standardize Advertising Spend and Sales Revenue
- Build a simple linear regression benchmark using scikit-learn
- Calculate benchmark Test RMSE and Test R²
- Implement gradient descent from scratch
- Learn the regression slope and intercept through iterative updates
- Compare three learning rates:
  - 0.001
  - 0.01
  - 0.10
- Compare final training cost, Test RMSE, Test R², slope, and intercept
- Visualize learning-rate convergence
- Compare gradient descent results with scikit-learn linear regression
- Fit a Ridge Regression model as an introduction to regularization
- Review and improve Copilot-generated code

## Analysis Includes
- Simple linear regression benchmark
- Gradient descent implementation
- Learning-rate comparison
- Convergence curves
- Model performance comparison
- Ridge Regression demonstration

## Files
- Python program for gradient descent and model comparison
- `learning_rate_comparison.csv`
- `model_comparison.csv`
- `learning_rate_convergence.png`
- Copilot code-review documentation
